{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness","id":1481035,"title":"Adapt a show or movie's setting to the World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-13T19:57:09-07:00","id":1481035,"title":"Adapt a show or movie's setting to the World of Darkness","content":"What the title says:<br /> <br /> <b>Stranger Things</b> is just straight up set in the World of Darkness with the Technocracy having a Construct there, a Progentior psychic experiment, and Void Engineers attempting to breach the Penumbra but attracting Nephandus/Wyrm creatures due to the cruelty of their human experimentation.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the Technocracy helps explain one of the sillier elements of season three as the Technocracy didn't think anything of using Correspondence &quot;Enlightened Science&quot; to move a large number of Russian assets to the area to resume their research as well as build a massive underground base under a mall despite the absurd impracticalities during the Cold War.<br /> <br /> Mind you, no one really wants to admit a bunch of frigging pre-teens helped bring down an entire Construct.<br /> <br /> Twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T01:04:57-07:00","id":1481348,"title":"","content":"I use a system of 'Eigenvectors' to analyse stories so that they can be replayed but in a different setting and with different characters. There are four types of colour-coded vectors - <span style=\"color:#006400\">Quest</span>, <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Hindrance</span>, <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Advantage</span>, and <span style=\"color:#B22222\">Adversary </span>(yes it was inspired by Fate Core), if you're interested in learning more I've got a document about it all. As there have been a number of films of this classic story I think it's suitable for inclusion.<br /> <br /> <b>Romeo and Juliet</b><br /> The protagonists and Romeo and Juliet and they share all eigenvectors unless otherwise noted. Both share an overall goal:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">[Quest - Two Houses Divided]</span><br /> Your house is at odds with another, do your best to avoid strife and bring them together.<br /> Blocked Reward: [Advantage - Two Houses United]<br /> Failure: [Two Houses at War]<br /> <br /> The setting is renaissance Italy, at night.<br /> <br /> <b>Act I</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">[Adversary - Toreador vs Tremere]</span><br /> You'd like to teach the other house's scions a lesson<br /> ST note - any combat leads to [Hindrance - On Pain of Death]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Hindrance - On Pain of Death]</span><br /> The Prince of the city has decreed that any further breach of the peace is punishable by death<br /> <br /> <b>Act II - Dream</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Juliet's Hindrance - Paris's Courtship]</span><br /> Your father, mother, and blood doll all think you should accept Count Paris's offer of marriage but you are not interested in him. You must find a way out before your parents force you into marriage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">[Romeo's Quest - Romeo and Rosaline]</span><br /> You have an unrequited infatuation with Rosaline, find a way to woo her.<br /> - Attempt to meet her at the Capulet ball while in disguise<br /> - Avoid Tybalt<br /> Leads to [True Love Quest - Romeo and Juliet]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">[True Love Quest - Romeo and Juliet]</span><br /> You must find a way to meet with your true love, woo them, and 'live happily ever after'<br /> - Balcony scene<br /> - Get married<br /> - Reveal your union at the right time and unite your houses<br /> Reward: finishing this quest unblocks the Reward for [Quest - Two houses Divided]<br /> <br /> <b>Act III - Frustration</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Hindrance \u2013 Star Cross'd Lovers]</span><br /> The Prince has banned all breaches of peace in the city so your love must remain secret lest your families fall into fighting<br /> Progress: Turn the card to gain 1xp and fill in one section of the progress bar whenever your secret love is almost exposed<br /> [ ] [ ] [ ]<br /> Completion: When all the sections are filled in or your secret is exposed, gain 3xp, discard (burn) this card, and replace it with [Hindrance \u2013 Two Houses at War]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">[Romeo's Ally - Mercutio]</span><br /> Your old friend and ally, will defend your honour to the death.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">[Romeo's Adversary - Tybalt]</span><br /> Incensed that you sneaked into the Tremere ball, Tybalt challenges you to a duel. You must find a way to make peace with him because if Tybalt dies there will be serious consequences.<br /> Reward: ???<br /> Failure: [Two Houses at War]<br /> <i>ST notes - possible outcomes:</i><br /> <i>- Romeo reveals his secret love, Mercutio defends him, Tybalt lives &gt; [Hindrance - Exiled]</i><br /> <i>- Romeo surrenders, Mercutio killed by Tybalt, Tybalt killed by Romeo &gt; [Hindrance - Exiled]</i><br /> <i>- Romeo kills Tybalt, escapes execution &gt; [Hindrance - Wanted]</i><br /> <i>- Mercutio kills Tybalt &gt; Mercutio executed and [Hindrance - Two Houses at War]</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Romeo's Hindrance - Exiled]</span><br /> You have been exiled from the city under penalty of death should you return.<br /> <br /> <b>Act IV - Nightmare</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Hindrance - Separated]</span><br /> You are separated by time and distance and can no longer find consolation in each other's arms<br /> <i>ST note - Our protagonists are now separated and can no longer share eigenvectors or information</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">[Juliet's Quest - Two and Forty hours]</span><br /> To avoid marriage to Paris you consult with Friar Laurence who teaches you a spell that will put you into torpor for two and forty hours while seemingly in final death. The Friar also promises to send a message to Romeo to come rescue you.<br /> Reward: destiny fulfilled<br /> <i>ST note - leads to [Quest - A Timeless End]</i><br /> <br /> Event - Juliet tcasts the spell and is placed in the family crypt but the Friar's message to Romeo is delayed by the rising sun<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">[Romeo's Ally - Balthasar]</span><br /> Upon hearing of Juliet's death your ally Balthasar rushes to your side to inform you. You must decide on a course of action, will it be vengeance or death? Leads to either [Hindrance - Two Houses at War] if you decide on vengeance, or [Quest - What ho, Apothecary!] if you decide that only death can reconcile your destiny.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">[Romeo's Quest - What ho, Apothecary!]</span><br /> Heartbroken you vow to die in Juliet's arms. Buy silver nitrate poison from an apothecary, sneak into the Capulet crypt, and lay to rest beside her.<br /> Reward: destiny fulfilled<br /> <i>ST note - leads to [Quest - A Timeless End]</i><br /> <br /> <b>Act V</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#006400\">[Juliet's Quest - A Timeless End]</span><br /> You awake to find Romeo beside you, dead by poison, and the sun slowly creeping through the door of the crypt. You must decide whether to live eternally without your true love or cast both of you into the sunlight.<br /> <i>ST note - leads to either [Advantage - Two houses United] or [Hindrance - Two Houses at War]</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">[Advantage - Two Houses United]</span><br /> Your two families are united.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DAA520\">[Hindrance - Two Houses at War]</span><br /> Your two families are at war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 05-18-2022, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T06:05:52-07:00","id":1481363,"title":"","content":"I have always thought that Yu-Gi-Oh (at least the original manga) would transplant pretty well, in a way. Most likely into Mage, though I'm not 100% familiar with that line. It would certainly explain what the ever loving fuck is wrong with the school population and 75% of people's parents, and why the laws of physics are constantly getting screwed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-18-2022, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-18T08:51:36-07:00","id":1481372,"title":"","content":"Ash Ketchum is a BSD theurge who always remains in homid while filming his live-action show about catching minor spirits and making them fight. Making them fight slowly corrupts the spirits into banes, while making a profit for Pentex and normalizing slavery and cruelty to the mainly young audience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-19T19:30:01-07:00","id":1481505,"title":"","content":"I was in a bar when I saw this thread. &quot;Ferris Buellers Day Off&quot; was playing on the TV.<br /> <br /> Ferris is some kind of Orphan - it would take magic for things to line up for him as nicely as they do. The principal is an Technocrat enlightened citizen exile dto the boonies for past fuck-ups. The sister eventually becomes an Euthanatos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T19:04:59-07:00","id":1481889,"title":"","content":"<b>Friday the 13th: The Series</b> is ... exactly the same as it is in the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:12:19-07:00","id":1482809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1481889#post1481889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Friday the 13th: The Series</b> is ... exactly the same as it is in the show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Canadian Content for the win!<br /> <br /> Shame they never got around to tieing into the movies as they planned. This is why &quot;In Medias Res&quot; is a thing; you insist on starting &quot;at the beginning,&quot; and you risk boring people away before you get to the good stuff. Hook people with the good stuff right away, and THEN you can go back &quot;to the beginning.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, I actually like the movie origin of the Hockey Mask, and it would also have been a shame if the series tried to retcon that, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T13:36:39-07:00","id":1482821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1482809#post1482809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Canadian Content for the win!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That show is probably largely responsible for my life long interests in history and supernatural horror. That and Frankenstein vs the Wolfman.<br /> <br /> I think the remake film ends up offering the best possibility for a crossover via Pamela's necklace. Say she killed the two councilors responsible for Jason's drowning the next summer, causing the camp to close. But it ultimately doesn't help her loss, and several years later, a depressed Pamela wanders into Louis's shop, where he sells her the necklace. It starts whispering to her in Jason's voice, eventually leading her back to Crystal Lake. There she finds out that they are planning to reopen the summer camp, and her own rage combined with the necklace's influence sends her on a murder spree. <br /> The necklace's power is, obviously, to bring back a deceased loved one, with the more murders you commit, the more &quot;real&quot; they become. (It's not really them though, just a simulation.) But Pamela's own death ends up being what brings this Jason fully to life. And he goes on to kill anyone intruding on his territory. His mother may whisper to him via the necklace, but the Jason doesn't have a soul to take so it has no need to bring back his mother and he's going to kill anyway. <br /> You could probably somehow tie this in with some stuff the comic books came up with, about the land around Crystal Lake being corrupted or cursed, similar to King's Pet Semitary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T13:44:06-07:00","id":1482823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness#post1481035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the title says:<br /> <br /> <b>Stranger Things</b> is just straight up set in the World of Darkness with the Technocracy having a Construct there, a Progentior psychic experiment, and Void Engineers attempting to breach the Penumbra but attracting Nephandus/Wyrm creatures due to the cruelty of their human experimentation.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the Technocracy helps explain one of the sillier elements of season three as the Technocracy didn't think anything of using Correspondence &quot;Enlightened Science&quot; to move a large number of Russian assets to the area to resume their research as well as build a massive underground base under a mall despite the absurd impracticalities during the Cold War.<br /> <br /> Mind you, no one really wants to admit a bunch of frigging pre-teens helped bring down an entire Construct.<br /> <br /> Twice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supernatural. I still maintain that the Winchesters are basically Amenti. They die and come back constantly, and they use a bit of magic combined with mundane weaponry to fight monsters. Also, they seem made for being worked into crossovers, which always seemed to be a Mummy thing for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T14:16:32-07:00","id":1482832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1482823#post1482823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Supernatural. I still maintain that the Winchesters are basically Amenti. They die and come back constantly, and they use a bit of magic combined with mundane weaponry to fight monsters. Also, they seem made for being worked into crossovers, which always seemed to be a Mummy thing for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much so that they make a cameo appearance in one of CE Murphy's The Walker Papers novels.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I could buy them as young immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T14:17:01-07:00","id":1482833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1482821#post1482821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That show is probably largely responsible for my life long interests in history and supernatural horror. That and Frankenstein vs the Wolfman.<br /> <br /> I think the remake film ends up offering the best possibility for a crossover via Pamela's necklace. Say she killed the two councilors responsible for Jason's drowning the next summer, causing the camp to close.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh, I guess, except it continues the trend of not giving Pamela Vorhees any credit.<br /> <br /> In the original Friday the 13th, as Annie is getting a ride, she's being told about all the things that happened BETWEEN the killing of the first two councilors and her hiring. The truck driver mentioned fires and sabotaged plumbing. Then, when Pam starts monologing about how she told Mr. Christie not to open the camp, you realize she's the one who's been sabotaging it to keep it closed. She only started killing again because sabotage didn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T14:24:03-07:00","id":1482835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481035-adapt-a-show-or-movie-s-setting-to-the-world-of-darkness?p=1482833#post1482833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sigh, I guess, except it continues the trend of not giving Pamela Vorhees any credit.<br /> <br /> In the original Friday the 13th, as Annie is getting a ride, she's being told about all the things that happened BETWEEN the killing of the first two councilors and her hiring. The truck driver mentioned fires and sabotaged plumbing. Then, when Pam starts monologing about how she told Mr. Christie not to open the camp, you realize she's the one who's been sabotaging it to keep it closed. She only started killing again because sabotage didn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I don't think the two need be mutually exclusive. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T15:18:08-07:00","id":1482839,"title":"","content":"There's basically two Friday: The Thirteenth ideas for a series with almost zero continuity:<br /> <br /> 1:] <b>Backwoods Psycho Jason</b>: Jason Voorhees didn't drown and he actually ended up swimming to shore before living in the woods for twenty years despite his various &quot;issues&quot;, becoming a feral wildman. This makes sense as campfire story logic but opens its own questions.<br /> <br /> 2:] <b>Jason X/Evil Dead Jason</b>: Pamela Voorhees somehow acquired the Necronomicon and proceeded to use the object to resurrect her dead son. Which has its own can of worms and insanity but would explain why Jason is a seemingly immortal killing machine.<br /> <br /> My preferred version for the World of Darkness is that Jason Voorhees did survive the events of his &quot;drowning&quot; and ended up possessed by something in the Lake that turned him into a Formor. I'm going to go with W:TA and suggest that he was Child of Gaia kinfolk as was Pamela.<br /> <br /> Surviving in the abandoned cabins on stolen food and dead animals, he was a fairly benign spirit or at least unimportant until Pamela Voorhees death. From there, the spirit inside him twisted and became malevolent and he began his killing spree. The legend of his evils combined with his weird connection to the Lake meant that when he was finally killed by adolescent Tommy Jarvis, he wasn't permanently slain and possessed a variety of people before being bonded with his original body.<br /> <br /> The merged spirit of the original Jason and the corrupted Wyrm spirit are impossible to separate now and it's difficult to say where one begins and the other ends. However, it's a LOT more powerful than it should be as its ability to stand up to Freddy Krueger, Dream Demon, shows. The only way to permanently slay Jason is cleanse the spirit of Crystal Lake itself of the taint involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T10:53:41-07:00","id":1483319,"title":"","content":"I would use:<br /> 1. Copland. A small town for cops sponsored by Pentex. They own a local supermarket, two gas stations, doctors, veterinarians and drugstores. They can provide free shooting range for cops and their families. They can create a small perfect world for tired police officers. And some of their own high level management (to let the cops know when to look the other way). They just made one mistake: chose an uncorrupted kinfolk/garou as their sherrif. Or maybe they did it on purpose trying to corrupt him.<br /> <br /> 2. Next of kin. The main character is a kinfolk who try to convince his garou family from the middle of nowhere that traditional bloodshed is not a good way to resolve conflicts in big city, even if it's personal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-07T18:39:25-07:00","id":1483354,"title":"","content":"My favorite movie of all time, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tFMo3UJ4B4g\" target=\"_blank\">Arrival</a>. Amy Adams' character is a translator for the Void Engineers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T13:29:11-07:00","id":1483399,"title":"","content":"&quot;Vanishing point&quot; (the original one, from 1971) - a Silent Strider takes a task to deliver a fetish but at some point he decides to use it for himself. During his journey he meets various creatures from other splats. Alternatively it could be Convoy or Smokey and the Bandit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-08T16:23:45-07:00","id":1483417,"title":"","content":"While the Weaver spared no effort in the annihilation of the Insect Changers, and subsequently had the Ananasi finish the remainder, they did not die completely, their bloodied survivors drifting through spiritual vistas of the Aetherial Realm until they reached the center of the Milky Way. As humanity reveled in newer and more sophisticated blessing of the Weaver with space travel and warps, the Insect Changers were waiting for them, having turned into true Space Monsters, bent on the annihilation of everything that the Weaver treasured - with humanity a definite priority, alongside their precious technology.<br /> <br /> Regrettably for the Red Talons and like minds, however, not only are all Changers like the Ananasi lumped in with them, they're not too keen on letting the planet off, either. As such, a great deal of gritted teeth cooperation gave rise to using whatever was available to defeat the resurgent Insect Changers. And a young Glass Walker might have the potential to do more against them than anyone thinks possible - save for one of the spider-changers, who sees something in her after escaping through the Umbra and Pattern Web from a disastrous attempt to strike at the Insects using a primarily human and VE fleet.<br /> <br /> (Aim for the Top/Gunbuster as a Werewolf game with elements from other games used sparingly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-09T00:53:25-07:00","id":1483446,"title":"","content":"Sneakers: about a group of Monkeywrenches trying to avoid the trap set by their former member.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":